    "result_text": "Each person's row now has a statement button, and `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the statements spec.\n\n**What a statement does:**\n- **Audit:** it writes `STATEMENT sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 name=\u2026 due-total=\u2026 claims=\u2026` using the sheet's today. Only open and settled claims count, so drafts and voided claims are left out of both the due-total and the claim count.\n- **Binding:** each counting claim is locked to the figure it shows at that moment, so later rate or grade changes no longer move it. Each later statement rebinds the claims that count then. Any claim that no longer counts goes back to following the rates.\n- **On screen:** each claim shows `claim-stated` yes/no. Each person shows `person-statement-count`, `person-stated-total` and `person-statement-date`, which are blank before the first statement.\n\n**How it's built:**\n- **Stored data:** a new migration, `V13__statement.sql`, adds a `statement` table and two columns on `claim`: `stated` and `stated_due`. Statements live in their own table rather than on the person record, so taking one doesn't count as an edit to that person.\n- **Server:** `ClaimService.statement` locks the sheet and works out the figures. A settled claim's frozen due always comes first, so a statement never changes it. It's served at `POST /api/sheets/{id}/people/{personId}/statement`. The people list now includes each person's statement count, last due-total and date.\n- **Front end:** a claim's due and each person's due-total now use the bound figure when there is one. If taking a statement fails, the row shows a `person-error` message.\n\n**Choices the request and the test left open \u2014 worth checking:**\n- **Voiding a bound claim:** the claim stays marked \"yes\" and keeps its bound figure on screen until the next statement, though it stops counting toward totals. The first test expects this.\n- **Settling a bound claim:** its frozen due is the bound figure rather than a fresh calculation from today's rates, so what it shows doesn't change when it's settled. The test doesn't cover this.\n- **Editing a bound claim's amount:** it keeps its bound figure until the next statement. The test doesn't cover this either.\n- **No rate in force:** if the person's grade has no rate today and none of their counting claims has a fixed or bound figure, the statement records `due-total=n/a`, matching how the screen already shows that case.",
